  "step_3": "The decision reason requires (1) computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes, (2) calculating differences from this level, and (3) preferring the lottery with the higher chance of positive differences. The individual does not reference any such calculation. Instead, they focus solely on the worst outcome in Lottery B and its psychological weight. The information considered by the individual (severity of the largest loss) is different from the information required by the reason (all outcomes, their mean, and deviations). The justification (avoiding a large loss) is also distinct from the rule of the reason (maximizing chance of positive deviation from an average outcome). There is no evidence that the individual computed or used the aspiration level of -3000 or compared deviations from it. In fact, the individual chooses A, while the reason would prefer B, which further suggests divergence. The reasoning process described is inconsistent with the decision reason.",
